    rdfs:subClassOf onto:Battery ;
    skos:altLabel "Lithium Battery"@en ;
    skos:definition "A battery which uses lithium ions as a key component of its electrochemistry using liquid electrolyte solutions. It consists of two current collectors, a negative and positive electrode, and a separator containing electrolytes. The primary lithium battery uses carbon fluoride, (CF)n, as a cathode and lithium metal as an anode. The negative electrode consists of either metallic lithium or lithium compounds."@en ;
