onto:ECTOS a onto:InfrastructureProject,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ECTOS"@en ;
    dcterms:references <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuel_Cell_Bus_Club#CUTE> ;
    onto:hasProject onto:Iceland ;
    onto:relatesToApplication <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Fuel_cell_bus> ;
    ns3:projectParticipant <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Icelandic_New_Energy> ;
    skos:altLabel "Ecological City Transport System"@en ;
    skos:definition "ECTOS stands for Ecological City Transport System.[15][16] Icelandic New Energy was responsible for this project, the aim of which was to demonstrate \"state-of-the-art\" hydrogen technology by running part of the public transport system with fuel cell buses in the city Reykjavík, the capital of Iceland. Hydrogen was produced from domestic geothermal and hydro-powered energy sources by electrolysis. The project ran from 2001-2005.[8]"@en .

