    dcterms:references <https://www.airbus.com/en/innovation/zero-emission/hydrogen/zeroe> ;
    onto:relatesToApplication onto:ZEROe ;
    onto:usesProduct <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hydrogen_Tank>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hydrogen_engine> ;
    skos:definition "Concept passenger aircraft. The exceptionally wide interior opens up multiple options for hydrogen storage and distribution. Here, the liquid hydrogen storage tanks are stored underneath the wings. Two hybrid-hydrogen turbofan engines provide thrust.\\r\\n\\r\\nRange: 2000nm\\r\\nPassengers: <200"@en .

